# Admin is a client-only SPA surface (robots-disallowed, behind auth).
/admin      /   200
/admin/*    /   200

# Blog posts are prerendered to their own HTML (US-WEB008), and Cloudflare
# Pages serves a matching static file before consulting this file. This rule
# is only reached by a post published since the last build — the generation
# webhook publishes straight to Supabase without a redeploy
# (docs/BLOG_GENERATION_WEBHOOK.md), so those must still render rather than
# 404. Serving the blog index shell lets React Router fetch and render the
# post client-side; the next build replaces it with real prerendered HTML.
# It must NOT point at `/`, which is what previously gave every post the
# homepage's title and canonical.
/blog/*     /blog/index.html   200
